BUILDING THREE TIER ARCHITECTURE ON AWS USING EKC(Elastic Kubernetes Service).

####____________COMPONENTS_______________####
1. Networking (VPC)
   - 1 VPC (10.0.0.0/16)
   - 2 Public Subnets (across 2 AZs) for the Load Balancer and NAT Gateway.
   - 2 Private Subnets (across 2 AZs) for the EKS Worker Nodes
   - 2 Private Subnets for the RDS Database.
   
2. Compute (EKS)
   - AWS manages the Control Plane.
   - We provision EC2 Worker Nodes in the private subnets to run our Pods.
   
3. Database (RDS)
   - PostgreSQL, deployed in the private database subnets (not accessible from the internet).
   
4. Container Registry (ECR)
   - Where are Docker Images li

5. CI/CD Pipeline (GitHub Actions)
   - Automatically build, test and deploy to EKS when we push to main

